 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with pauses of 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds between
+attempts. A successful capture returns immediately; a timeout on the final attempt is raised to the caller.
+The pauses can add up to 20 seconds to the member's wait on the confirmation page, in addition to gateway response
+time.
+
+During the gateway's Friday peak, 17:00 to 19:00, the previous three attempts ran within a second and hit the same
+slow period. One Friday left 58 confirmed pantry orders needing manual capture the next morning. Replaying those
+timeouts in the sandbox with the longer retry schedule would have captured 57 of the 58. The team accepted the
+longer confirmation wait to reduce that manual work; switching gateways was ruled out while the contract ran to
+December 2026. [Issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md) records the discussion.
 
